    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{a}{4}=a\\div4=a\\times\\frac14=\\frac14a$, so both answers are equivalent.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{11a}{4}-\\frac{5a}{2}&=\\frac{11a}{4}-\\frac{10a}{4}\\\\&=\\frac{a}{4}\\end{align*}$$\nDividing by $4$ is the same as multiplying by $\\frac14$, so $\\frac{a}{4}=\\frac14a$. Both are correct.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
